```python
from pycparser import c_parser, c_ast, parse_file, c_generator


def traverse(node: c_ast.Node, visitor):
    if isinstance(node, c_ast.FuncDef):
        for block in node.body.block_items:
            if isinstance(block, c_ast.Comment):
                visitor(node, block)
            else:
              traverse(block, visitor)


def generate_assert_statements(node: c_ast.Node, block: c_ast.Comment):
    if block.text.strip().startswith("@@@"):
       # TODO: Generate debug assertion statement, may need to extract condition
       pass


def process_file(file_path: str):
    ast = parse_file(file_path, use_cpp=True)
    traverse(ast, generate_assert_statements)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    # You need to replace this file path with your input file path
    process_file('/path/to/your/file.c')
```

This script will search for all function definitions in a file that contain comments starting with "@@@" and print information about each match. You have to modify `generate_assert_statements` to generate actual Debug.Assert statements.--------------------For the second code example, the output of assert statements will be:

